 guidance, forecast or event-progress statement, an official confirms or denies that reported claim, or the original source revises it; another statement on the same topic is not this\"}, \"instructions\": \"How does the INCOMING PIECE relate to the STORED PIECE below? Use only the supplied text. STORED PIECE:\\nSTORED PIECE [fact; Manali Pradhan, fool.com; original source Nvidia, stated unknown] Nvidia reported fiscal 2027 second-quarter revenue of $96.2 billion, up 106% year over year, including $89 billion in data center segment sales. The quarter ended July 26, 2026. | quote: In its fiscal 2027 second quarter (which ended July 26), Nvidia's revenue soared by 106% year over year to $96.2 billion, including $89 billion in sales from the data center segment.\", \"type\": \"choice\"}, \"q8\": {\"criteria\": {\"different\": \"a different fact, figure or matter, a figure for another period or quantity, or only a secondary statement of the stored piece, even if on the same topic\", \"same_statement\": \"the INCOMING PIECE reports the STORED PIECE's main statement: a retelling, another outlet carrying it, the same number in text or a table, or the same speaker repeating it; wording, precision and extra detail may differ. If the stored piece carries several statements and the incoming piece reports only a secondary one, this is not it\", \"supersedes\": \"a later version of the stored piece's main statement, changed: the same speaker revises that guidance, forecast or event-progress statement, an official confirms or denies that reported claim, or the original source revises it; another statement on the same topic is not this\"}, \"instructions\": \"How does the INCOMING PIECE relate to the STORED PIECE below? Use only the supplied text. STORED PIECE:\\nSTORED PIECE [party_statement; Manali Pradhan, fool.com; original source Nvidia, stated unknown] Nvidia management estimates its revenue opportunity per gigawatt of AI infrastructure has risen from roughly $18 billion with Hopper GPUs to $25 billion with Blackwell systems and $40 billion with Vera Rubin systems, partly because it sells more system components including CPUs, GPUs, NVLink and networking products. | quote: Nvidia is also expanding its revenue opportunity from each gigawatt (power capacity) of AI infrastructure. Management estimates that this opportunity has increased from roughly $18 billion with Hopper GPUs to $25 billion with Blackwell systems and $40 billion with Vera Rubin systems. These increases are partly a result of the fact that Nvidia is selling more components of the overall AI system, including CPUs, GPUs, NVLink (Nvidia's high-speed technology for connecting GPUs and other processors), and other networking products.\", \"type\": \"choice\"}, \"q9\": {\"criteria\": {\"different\": \"a different fact, figure or matter, a figure for another period or quantity, or only a secondary statement of the stored piece, even if on the same topic\", \"same_statement\": \"the INCOMING PIECE reports the STORED PIECE's main statement: a retelling, another outlet carrying it, the same number in text or a table, or the same speaker repeating it; wording, precision and extra detail may differ. If the stored piece carries several statements and the incoming piece reports only a secondary one, this is not it\", \"supersedes\": \"a later version of the stored piece's main statement, changed: the same speaker revises that guidance, forecast or event-progress statement, an official confirms or denies that reported claim, or the original source revises it; another statement on the same topic is not this\"}, \"instructions\": \"How does the INCOMING PIECE relate to the STORED PIECE below? Use only the supplied text. STORED PIECE:\\nSTORED PIECE [party_statement; Manali Pradhan, fool.com; original source Nvidia, stated unknown] Nvidia expects the combined capital expenditures of the top five hyperscalers to approach $800 billion in calendar 2026 and $1.3 trillion in calendar 2027. | quote: Nvidia also expects the combined capital expenditures of the top five hyperscalers to approach $800 billion in 2026 and $1.3 trillion in 2027.\", \"type\": \"choice\"}}, \"state\": \"INCOMING PIECE [fact; indexbox.io, citing EU Tech Loop and Euronews; original source NVIDIA, stated Thursday] Nvidia announced on Thursday that it is acquiring the open-source AI model repository Hugging Face for $13 billion (EUR 11.2 billion). The item gives no closing date and attributes the report to EU Tech Loop and Euronews; it does not say whether the deal has regulatory approval. | quote: American chipmaker NVIDIA announced on Thursday its acquisition of the artificial intelligence library Hugging Face for $13 billion (EUR11.2bn). The deal, reported by EU Tech Loop and shared on Euronews, marks a significant investment in a platform that began as a chat app for teenagers and evolved into a major repository for open-source and open-weight AI models.\"}",
