76	      "jev_full": "{\"model\": \"jev-1.14.0\", \"questions\": {\"q0\": {\"criteria\": {\"different\": \"a different fact, figure or matter, a figure for another period or quantity, or only a secondary statement of the stored piece, even if on the same topic\", \"same_statement\": \"the INCOMING PIECE reports the STORED PIECE's main statement: a retelling, another outlet carrying it, the same number in text or a table, or the same speaker repeating it; wording, precision and extra detail may differ. If the stored piece carries several statements and the incoming piece reports only a secondary one, this is not it\", \"supersedes\": \"a later version of the stored piece's main statement, changed: the same speaker revises that guidance, forecast or event-progress statement, an official confirms or denies that reported claim, or the original source revises it; another statement on the same topic is not this\"}, \"instructions\": \"How does the INCOMING PIECE relate to the STORED PIECE below? Use only the supplied text. STORED PIECE:\\nSTORED PIECE [rumour; Pocket-lint (Craig Donaldson), citing AFTV News; original source Nvidia, stated unknown] Nvidia appears to have quietly discontinued its standard (tube-shaped) $150 Shield TV streaming device, according to Pocket-lint (citing AFTV News): the unit is no longer purchasable directly from Nvidia or at most major retailers, with authorized dealer B&H Photo Video listing it as 'Discontinued', Best Buy saying it is 'no longer available in new condition' and Newegg saying it is out of stock and may or may not be restocked. Pocket-lint had no official confirmation from Nvidia, said it had asked the company, and noted the $200 Shield TV Pro remains on sale. The item leaves open that this could simply be an out-of-stock situation. | quote: Unfortunately, it now appears that the cheaper Shield TV's time on the market has come to an end, as Nvidia seems to have quietly discontinued it (via AFTV News ). The Shield TV is no longer available to purchase directly from Nvidia, and the same is true across most major retailers. In particular, B&H Photo Video , an Nvidia-authorized dealer, lists the Shield TV as \\\"Discontinued\\\" on its product page (as you can see in the image above). Best Buy doesn't go quite that far, but if you try to buy the streamer new, it says, \\\"This item is no longer available in new condition.\\\" Newegg has a similarly discouraging message, stating, \\\"This item is currently out of stock and it may or may not be restocked.\\\" Pocket-lint has reached out to Nvidia for official confirmation on whether the Shield TV has been discontinued, and we'll update this story if we hear back.\", \"type\": \"choice\"}, \"q1\": {\"criteria\": {\"different\": \"a different fact, figure or matter, a figure for another period or quantity, or only a secondary statement of the stored piece, even if on the same topic\", \"same_statement\": \"the INCOMING PIECE reports the STORED PIECE's main statement: a retelling, another outlet carrying it, the same number in text or a table, or the same speaker repeating it; wording, precision and extra detail may differ. If the stored piece carries several statements and the incoming piece reports only a secondary one, this is not it\", \"supersedes\": \"a later version of the stored piece's main statement, changed: the same speaker revises that guidance, forecast or event-progress statement, an official confirms or denies that reported claim, or the original source revises it; another statement on the same topic is not this\"}, \"instructions\": \"How does the INCOMING PIECE relate to the STORED PIECE below? Use only the supplied text. STORED PIECE:\\nSTORED PIECE [rumour; tech-insider.org, citing supply-chain sources; original source NVIDIA, stated unknown] According to supply-chain reporting summarized in the item, NVIDIA has pulled the RTX 5060 from retail and cut production of existing RTX 50-series cards by an estimated 15% to 20% through 