 the first time in close to three decades, Nvidia is not shipping a new gaming GPU architecture in a calendar year. Nvidia has shipped zero new gaming GPU architectures through September 2026 , breaking a release streak dating back roughly 30 years to the GeForce 256 in 1999.\", \"type\": \"choice\"}, \"q3\": {\"criteria\": {\"different\": \"a different fact, figure or matter, a figure for another period or quantity, or only a secondary statement of the stored piece, even if on the same topic\", \"same_statement\": \"the INCOMING PIECE reports the STORED PIECE's main statement: a retelling, another outlet carrying it, the same number in text or a table, or the same speaker repeating it; wording, precision and extra detail may differ. If the stored piece carries several statements and the incoming piece reports only a secondary one, this is not it\", \"supersedes\": \"a later version of the stored piece's main statement, changed: the same speaker revises that guidance, forecast or event-progress statement, an official confirms or denies that reported claim, or the original source revises it; another statement on the same topic is not this\"}, \"instructions\": \"How does the INCOMING PIECE relate to the STORED PIECE below? Use only the supplied text. STORED PIECE:\\nSTORED PIECE [fact; The Information (cited by tech-insider.org); original source NVIDIA, as reported by The Information, stated December 2025 (shelving)] According to The Information, NVIDIA shelved its entire planned RTX 50 \\\"Super\\\" refresh in December 2025, including a 24GB RTX 5080 Super that had reached a completed-design stage. The card will not be manufactured, at least not in 2026, because the GDDR7 modules it requires are being allocated to higher-margin AI and data-center products. | quote: The planned RTX 5080 Super (24GB) reached a completed-design stage before Nvidia shelved the entire RTX 50 Super refresh in December 2025 . The card will not be manufactured, at least not in 2026, because