ge calculator lists three unannounced Nvidia GeForce RTX 50 Super graphics cards — an RTX 5080 Super, an RTX 5070 Ti Super, and an RTX 5070 Super (the item's text repeats 'RTX 5070 Ti Super') — as selectable options, which the article treats as a sign that a mid-cycle RTX 50 Super refresh could still happen at some point. The products are unconfirmed by Nvidia, and the article notes that none of its trade-show conversations suggest such a refresh will occur any time soon. | quote: But there are still signs that such an update could still happen at some point, and the latest sign comes from Seasonic, which has listed an RTX 5080 Super, an RTX 5070 Ti Super, and RTX 5070 Ti Super in its PSU wattage calculator . You can click through the calculator and assemble a hypothetical system with these unannounced products inside. The GeForce RTX 50-series desktop graphics lineup has remained unchanged for just over a year now (since the introduction of the RTX 5050), and none of the conversations we've had at major trade shows suggests that a mid-cycle Super refresh will occur any time soon.\", \"type\": \"choice\"}}, \"state\": \"INCOMING PIECE [party_statement; Pocket-lint (Craig Donaldson); original source Nvidia, stated unknown] Responding by email to Pocket-lint's inquiry about the future of the Shield TV, Nvidia said the SHIELD TV base model is largely out of stock due to demand, that it has no updates to share on future availability, that SHIELD TV Pro remains available, and that the SHIELD platform continues to be supported with ongoing updates for more than 10 years; Nvidia would neither confirm nor deny that the base model has been discontinued. | quote: Pocket-lint reached out to Nvidia for clarification on the Shield TV's future and received an email response. Here's what Nvidia had to say: \\\"The SHIELD TV base model is largely out of stock due to demand. We don't have any updates to share regarding future availability at this time. SHIELD TV Pro remains available, and the SHIELD platform continues to be supported with ongoing updates for more than 10 years.\\\" While Nvidia confirmed that the base Shield TV is out of stock due to demand, what's still unclear is what happens next.\"}",
